{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.InterfaceKnotMarkovZ","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.InterfaceKnotMarkovZ","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.markovZD_lt_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.markovZD_lt_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":512,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L512-L516","doc":"**Convention-D Markov parameter below 1.**  For `q > 0`,\n`q³/(q² + 1) < 1 ↔ q³ < q² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.markovParam_le_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.markovParam_le_half","kind":"theorem","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L507-L510","doc":"AM-GM: `1/(t + t⁻¹) ≤ 1/2` for `t > 0`.  This bounds the convention-C expression\n`1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})`, not the canonical convention-D parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.two_le_add_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.two_le_add_inv","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L501-L505","doc":"For `t > 0`, `t + t⁻¹ ≥ 2` (AM-GM, from `(t-1)² ≥ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.productModel_3body_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.productModel_3body_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L465-L484","doc":"**Product-model many-body obstruction (the real result).** For the\nmultiplicative model `B(S) = c·(1 − ∏_{i∈S} fᵢ)` with `c ≥ 0` and every\n`fᵢ ∈ [0,1]`, the *physical* beyond-pairwise 3-body content\n`B(abc) − [B(a)+B(b)+B(c)] = c·(f_a+f_b+f_c − f_a f_b f_c − 2)` is\n**non-positive**.  So a saturating interface product — signed closed-form\ntrace or `|χ|` combiner alike — can **never** produce an attractive (`> 0`)\n3-body force; that requires a non-multiplicative / cooperative combiner\n(one with an enhancing `fᵢ > 1` interface, or a genuine 3-body operator that\nis not a product of pairwise factors).  This is the correctly-scoped\nstructural fact behind the retracted \"triangle sign flip\": the per-cluster\nsigns alternate, but their *sum* is bounded `≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.ursell3_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.ursell3_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L454-L463","doc":"**Odd bond-count → non-negative.** The *isolated* 3-bond cluster\n`+c(1−fₐ)(1−f_b)(1−f_c) ≥ 0` for `c ≥ 0`, `fₐ,f_b,f_c ≤ 1`.  This is the sign\nof the single top cluster term only; the physical beyond-pairwise 3-body\ncontent (this `+` term plus the negative 2-bond clusters) is destructive\n(`< 0`), so this lemma does NOT establish an attractive 3-body force (see the\nscope caveat above). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.ursell2_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.ursell2_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L446-L452","doc":"**Even bond-count → non-positive.** The 2-bond cluster `−c(1−fₐ)(1−f_b) ≤ 0`\nfor `c ≥ 0`, `fₐ,f_b ≤ 1` — the saturation sign (destructive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.ursell3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.ursell3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":439,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L439-L444","doc":"3-bond (triangle) connected cluster (product model) `= +c(1−fₐ)(1−f_b)(1−f_c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.ursell2_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.ursell2_eq","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L434-L437","doc":"2-bond connected cluster (product model) `= −c(1−fₐ)(1−f_b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.cluster2_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.cluster2_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":411,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L411-L415","doc":"The cluster vanishes exactly when the joint trace factorises additively\n(`g∅ + g_ab = gₐ + g_b`): no irreducible 3-body content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.cluster2_eq_joint_sub_pairsum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.cluster2_eq_joint_sub_pairsum","kind":"theorem","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L403-L409","doc":"The connected cluster equals (joint binding) − (independent pair-sum):\nwith `joint = g∅ − g_ab` and `pair_sum = (g∅−gₐ)+(g∅−g_b)`,\n`cluster2 = joint − pair_sum`. The irreducible 3-body term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.cluster2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Cluster.cluster2","kind":"def","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L400-L401","doc":"Connected 2-bond (Ursell) cluster from the four interface sub-traces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SU4Supermultiplet.su4_last_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SU4Supermultiplet.su4_last_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L373-L376","doc":"Contrapositive: a nonzero `[1^A]` supermultiplet forces `A ≤ 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SU4Supermultiplet.helium4_singlet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SU4Supermultiplet.helium4_singlet","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L369-L371","doc":"⁴He (A=4) is the last nonzero antisymmetric supermultiplet: the SU(4) singlet,\ndimension 1 (the doubly-magic alpha, `S=0, T=0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SU4Supermultiplet.su4_shell_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SU4Supermultiplet.su4_shell_closure","kind":"theorem","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L363-L367","doc":"**SU(4) shell closure.** The fully-antisymmetric supermultiplet `[1^A]`\nvanishes for `A > 4`: no Pauli-allowed spin-isospin-antisymmetric state of\nmore than 4 nucleons exists in the s-shell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SU4Supermultiplet.su4AntisymDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SU4Supermultiplet.su4AntisymDim","kind":"def","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L359-L361","doc":"Dimension of the fully-antisymmetric SU(4) spin-isospin supermultiplet\n`[1^A] = Λ^A(ℂ⁴)`:  `C(4, A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit_marginal_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit_marginal_le","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L331-L343","doc":"**Saturation.** The marginal deficit of adding bond `f` is `(1−f)·∏`, hence\n`≤ (1−f)`: each added bond contributes at most its bare deficit, and strictly\nless once other bonds are present (`∏ < 1`).  This is *why* extra bonds barely\nmove `B` — the correctly-scoped statement of the 4-body assembly result (the\ninterface program is not excluded; the multiplicative deficit just saturates). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit_cons_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit_cons_ge","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L322-L329","doc":"Monotone: adding a bond `f ∈ [0,1]` never decreases the deficit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L318-L320","doc":"`D ≤ 1`: the multiplicative deficit can never exceed 1 — it **saturates**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L314-L316","doc":"`0 ≤ D` for factors in `[0,1]` (the deficit is a genuine non-negative shortfall). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.deficit","kind":"def","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L311-L312","doc":"The interface deficit of a bond-factor list: `D = 1 − ∏ f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.prod_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.prod_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L297-L309","doc":"A product of factors each in `[0,1]` is `≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.prod_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceDeficit.prod_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L289-L295","doc":"A product of factors each `≥ 0` is `≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z_per_Z_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z_per_Z_step","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L263-L273","doc":"**Per-Z step factorisation**: for the per-Z-step transition\n(Z, N) → (Z+1, N), the new interface is a *positive* generator\n(p-p or p-n boundary), contributing a factor of `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z_bar_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z_bar_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L225-L259","doc":"**Bar-invariant (p-n) interface Markov identity.**\n\nThe canonical p-n boundary in `closed_form_tau_M.canonical_interface_kinds`\nis the *bar-invariant* (charge-symmetric) crossing\n  σ_bar := σ + σ⁻¹ = 2σ - h·1      (from the Hecke skein σ⁻¹ = σ - h·1),\ni.e. the q ↔ q⁻¹–symmetric average of the positive and negative crossings\n(no preferred chirality at the p-n bond).  Its Markov trace is\n\n  τ_M(α · (σ + σ⁻¹)) = (2z - h) · τ_M(α),\n\nso the per-interface \"averaged\" factor (after the 1/2 normalisation that\nlives at the archimedean realisation) is `z - h/2`.  Together with the\npositive (`z`) and negative (`z - h`) identities above, this shows all\nTHREE interface factors are forced by **one** Markov move\n`τ_M(α·σ) = z·τ_M(α)` plus the skein — no fit (cf. `prop:averaging-resonance-rule`).\n\nStated division-free over a generic `CommRing R` (the 1/2 is deferred to\nthe archimedean step, per AGENTS.md §7c base-ring convention). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z_negative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z_negative","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L196-L221","doc":"**Negative-interface Markov-Hecke identity**: for a negative\ninterface generator σ⁻¹ (corresponding to an n-n boundary in\nthe canonical atomic braid), the Markov trace ratio is\n`(z - h)`, NOT `z`.\n\nProof: by Hecke skein, σ⁻¹ = σ - h·1, so\n  τ_M(α · σ⁻¹) = τ_M(α · σ - α · h · 1)\n                = τ_M(α · σ) - h · τ_M(α)\n                = z · τ_M(α) - h · τ_M(α)\n                = (z - h) · τ_M(α). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.hecke_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.hecke_skein","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L191-L191","doc":"Hecke skein relation: σ⁻¹ = σ - h·1 on interface generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.sigma_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.sigma_inv","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L189-L189","doc":"Inverse of an interface generator (in the abstract algebra). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.h","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L187-L187","doc":"The Hecke skein parameter h ∈ R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L184-L184","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.toMarkovTraceAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra.toMarkovTraceAlgebra","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L184-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovHeckeSkeinAlgebra","kind":"class","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L175-L194","doc":"**Markov-Hecke-skein algebra**: an extension of `MarkovTraceAlgebra`\nthat also carries the Hecke skein parameter `h` and the skein\nrelation `σ⁻¹ = σ - h·1` on interface generators.  This lets us\ncompute the Markov trace of `α · σ⁻¹` from the Markov axiom on\n`α · σ`.\n\nIn the concrete Hecke setting H_n(q), `h = q - q⁻¹` and the\nskein relation is the canonical defining identity of the\nIwahori-Hecke algebra (per AGENTS.md §7a). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L153-L171","doc":"**Iterated interface-knot factorisation.**  Folding the per-interface\nfactors over the constituent vacuum yields the closed product\n\n  τ_M(β_K) = z^{p_+} · (z - h)^{p_-} · τ_M(β_K^vac),\n\nwhere `p_+ = signs.count true` (positive interfaces) and\n`p_- = signs.count false` (negative interfaces).  Proved by induction on the\ninterface list from the two single-step identities — no `sorry`, no extra\nhypotheses (the division-free product form; cf. the malformed ratio\nplaceholder it replaces). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:interface-knot-markov-z","label":"prop:interface-knot-markov-z","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.interfaceTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.interfaceTrace","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L142-L150","doc":"`interfaceTrace z h tvac signs` folds the interface knot `bowtie_K` onto the\nconstituent-vacuum trace `tvac = τ_M(β_K^vac)`: each *positive* interface\n(`true`) multiplies the running trace by `z` (Markov axiom), each *negative*\ninterface (`false`) by `z - h` (Markov axiom + Hecke skein).  This is exactly\n`τ_M(β_K)` assembled from the two single-step identities\n`interface_knot_markov_z_single` and `interface_knot_markov_z_negative`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z_single","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L104-L140","doc":"**Interface-knot Markov-z theorem (single-step).**\n\nFor a canonical atomic braid `β_K = α · σ` where σ is the\ninterface generator at a strand-block boundary and α is the\nsub-braid below the boundary, the Markov trace ratio between\nthe bound atom β_K and the constituent sub-braid α equals the\nMarkov parameter z exactly:\n\n  τ_M(α · σ) / τ_M(α) = z.\n\nThis is just the Markov axiom for the canonical Markov trace\napplied at the interface generator.\n\n**Value.**  Under convention D, z(q) = q³/(q² + 1), so\nz(q₀) ≈ 0.6127 at the proton pin.  (An earlier version quoted\n0.49932, the excised convention-C value 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2}).)\n\n**Structural reading.**  The interface knot Δ_I^K of PR #801 is\n*categorically the Markov-axiom boundary contribution* to the\ncanonical atomic braid.  It is not phenomenological or a fit\nparameter — it is the direct algebraic consequence of the\ncanonical Markov trace's defining property on H_n(q).\n\nEquivalently: each interface generator at a strand-block\nboundary contributes a factor of z to the total Markov trace,\nso a canonical atomic braid with A nucleons has\n\n    τ_M(β_K) = z^(A-1) · τ_M(β_K^constit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.markov_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.markov_axiom","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L96-L96","doc":"**Markov axiom** (the defining property of τ_M).\n\nThe single-step version: for an interface generator σ and any\nα living below σ, multiplying α by σ on the right multiplies\nthe Markov trace by z. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.isBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.isBelow","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Test predicate: does α \"live below\" σ?  In the concrete Hecke\nsetting, this is true iff α ∈ H_{n-1} under the standard\ninclusion ignoring strand n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.isInterface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.isInterface","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Test predicate: is σ an \"interface generator\" suitable for the\nMarkov axiom? In the concrete Hecke setting, this is true iff\nσ = σ_{n-1} for some n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.tau_M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.tau_M","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The Markov trace τ_M : R → R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.z","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The Markov parameter z ∈ R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAlgebra","kind":"class","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/interface-knot-markov-z.lean#L64-L100","doc":"An abstract Markov-trace algebra is a triple (R, τ_M, z) where\nR is a commutative ring, z ∈ R is a fixed element (the Markov\nparameter), and τ_M : R → R is a function satisfying the\n**Markov axiom**: for \"boundary-interface\" elements σ ∈ R, and\nany α ∈ R that \"lives below the boundary\",\n\n  τ_M(α * σ) = z * τ_M(α).\n\nIn the QOU setting, R is the Hecke algebra H_n(q), σ is an\ninterface generator σ_g at a strand-block boundary, and α is\nthe constituent braid restricted to the strand-block below g.\n\nThe class abstracts the Markov-axiom side without committing to\na particular concrete Hecke-algebra implementation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}